(footprint "Supercap_Radial_D8.0mm_L12.0mm_P3.50mm_Horizontal"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Cylindrical radial EDLC supercapacitor mounted HORIZONTALLY: the two radial leads (0.6 mm, 3.50 mm pitch) exit the end face at the can's mid-height and bend 90 deg down to the pads 2.5 mm in front of the face; the can lies toward +X from the pads, with pad 1 at -Y. That is the opposite bend to Supercap_Radial_D10.0mm_L20.0mm_P5.00mm_Horizontal (can toward -X, same pad order): the same footprint turned half a turn would swap the + and - sides, this bend keeps them. Can 8.0 mm dia x 12.0 mm long nominal, lying on the board (8.0 mm tall); the CDA drawing allows D +/-1.0 and L +/-1.5, so up to 9.0 mm tall and 13.5 mm long (the body then ends 16.0 mm from the pads). Drawn for CDA/Zhifengwei CXHP2R7205R-TW (2.0 F, 2.7 V; ESR 100 mohm @1 kHz / 280 mohm DC), the Tinker-Mantis C130, which stands it on Supercap_Radial_D8.0mm_H12.0mm_P3.50mm. Drill 0.9 mm gives 0.3 mm clearance on the lead. Pad 1 = POSITIVE. *** DELIBERATELY NO COURTYARD OVER THE BODY *** - the can is glued down and may lie over other components, so the only keep-out is a small courtyard around the two legs, as on the 10 mm footprint. The body outline (nominal 12 mm) is on F.Fab as documentation only and generates no DRC. MECHANICAL: the 3D model rests the can on the board; parts under it must clear its underside, and parts under the 2.5 mm lead bend must stay low, since the lead descends there from the can's 4.0 mm mid-height. Datasheet: CDA CXHP(2.7V) Series, spec date 2022-06-10.")
	(tags "supercapacitor EDLC radial horizontal lay-down bent-lead glued no-keepout tht polarised CXHP2R7205R")
